%% OSPP Session Lifecycle State Machine
%% Reference: spec/05-state-machines.md, Section 3

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Pending : Session initiated<br/>(user requests session)

    Pending --> Authorized : Payment/credits verified
    Pending --> Failed : Payment declined<br/>Insufficient funds

    Authorized --> Active : StartService accepted<br/>by station
    Authorized --> Active : SessionStarted EVENT [MSG-043]<br/>(Partial B)
    Authorized --> Failed : StartService rejected<br/>or timeout (10s)
    Authorized --> Failed : Partial B start not reported<br/>within 40s

    Active --> Stopping : StopService requested<br/>(user, server, or timer)
    Active --> Completed : SessionEnded EVENT [MSG-040]<br/>(Local, LocalOutOfCredit, OperatorStopped)
    Active --> Failed : SessionEnded EVENT [MSG-040] Fault<br/>(hardware, or a restart not resumed),<br/>Deauthorized (RevocationEpoch bump)
    Active --> Completed : No end record by the sweep deadline,<br/>station away (not Partial B), marked as an anomaly
    Active --> Completed : No end record by the sweep deadline,<br/>station connected, marked as an anomaly
    Active --> Completed : Partial B authorized duration ended<br/>with no end record

    Stopping --> Completed : Station confirms stop<br/>StopService RESPONSE (user stop)<br/>or SessionEnded EVENT [MSG-040] (timer expiry)
    Stopping --> Completed : SessionEnded after a refused stop,<br/>or no end record by the sweep deadline
    Stopping --> Failed : SessionEnded Fault or Deauthorized<br/>after a refused stop

    Completed --> [*]
    Failed --> [*]

    state Pending {
        [*] --> VerifyingPayment
        VerifyingPayment --> CreditCheck : Wallet payment
        VerifyingPayment --> CardCapture : Card payment
    }

    state Active {
        [*] --> Dispensing
        Dispensing --> Dispensing : MeterValues<br/>(every MeterValuesInterval (default 60s))
    }

    note right of Pending
        Timeout: 10s
        No service delivered yet
    end note

    note right of Active
        MeterValues reported periodically
        Max duration: configurable (default 600s)
        Implementation detail: actual substates
        (VerifyingPayment, CreditCheck, CardCapture,
        Dispensing) vary by station type and payment
        processor. These are illustrative, not normative.
    end note

    note right of Completed
        Receipt generated
        Wallet debited for actual usage
        Unused credits refunded
        No end record by the sweep deadline (not Partial B): no refund,
        the full amount charged, the close marked as an anomaly
    end note

    note right of Failed
        Refund initiated if payment was captured
        SessionEnded Fault: settled by the Fault row
    end note
